format 1
adapter chat 1
npc: npc-ray

node chat-ray-greeting
kind: greeting
pose: greet
title: Chat

    Ray.

    Clipboard's out. Status?

reply: on track -> chat-ray-ontrack
reply: behind -> chat-ray-behind
reply: stuck -> chat-ray-stuck
reply: just talking -> chat-ray-talk
reply: gotta go -> chat-ray-bye

node chat-ray-menu
kind: reply
pose: idle

    Again. Status?

    On track, behind, stuck, talking or leaving. Pick one.

reply: on track -> chat-ray-ontrack
reply: behind -> chat-ray-behind
reply: stuck -> chat-ray-stuck
reply: just talking -> chat-ray-talk
reply: gotta go -> chat-ray-bye

node chat-ray-ontrack
kind: reply
pose: proud

    Good. Noted.

    Next job is on the map. Go do it.

link: Take me there => next-lesson
reply: quiz me first -> chat-ray-quiz
reply: later -> chat-ray-menu

node chat-ray-behind
kind: reply
pose: point

    Fine. Behind is a position. Not a verdict.

    Plan: one lesson. That's all. Then we recount.

link: Take me there => next-lesson
reply: ok, one lesson -> chat-ray-bye
reply: what if I'm too tired -> chat-ray-tired

node chat-ray-tired
kind: reply
pose: think

    Then do a short thing. A quiz. Five minutes.

    A short thing counts. Checked off is checked off.

link: A quick round => mythbuster radiation-meets-matter
reply: ok, fair -> chat-ray-menu

node chat-ray-quiz
kind: reply
pose: explain

    A round of Myth Buster. Radiation and matter.

    Fair questions. Short. Go.

link: Start the round => mythbuster radiation-meets-matter
reply: not now -> chat-ray-menu

node chat-ray-stuck
kind: reply
pose: think

    Stuck where? Name it. I'll give you the short version.

reply: what stops what -> chat-ray-r-stops
reply: exposed or contaminated -> chat-ray-r-contam
reply: ionizing or not -> chat-ray-r-ion
reply: the units -> chat-ray-r-units
reply: never mind -> chat-ray-menu

node chat-ray-r-stops
kind: reply
pose: explain

    Alpha: paper, or the outer layer of skin.

    Beta: a thin layer of metal.

    Gamma: several inches of lead, or a few feet of concrete.

    Three kinds. Three different stoppers.

link: Open it in AtomDex => entry shielding
reply: thanks, back -> chat-ray-menu

node chat-ray-r-contam
kind: reply
pose: explain

    Exposed: you're in the path of radiation from a source.

    Contaminated: radioactive material is on you or in you.

    Radiation doesn't spread. The material does.

link: Open it in AtomDex => entry radioactive-contamination
reply: thanks, back -> chat-ray-menu

node chat-ray-r-ion
kind: reply
pose: explain

    Ionizing: enough energy to knock electrons out of atoms. X-rays, gamma rays, alpha and beta.

    Non-ionizing: radio waves, microwaves, visible light.

link: Open it in AtomDex => entry ionizing-radiation
reply: thanks, back -> chat-ray-menu

node chat-ray-r-units
kind: reply
pose: explain

    Becquerel: decays per second of a source.

    Gray: energy absorbed per kilogram.

    Sievert: potential for harm.

    Different questions. Don't swap them.

link: Open it in AtomDex => entry sievert
reply: thanks, back -> chat-ray-menu

node chat-ray-talk
kind: reply
pose: greet

    Fine. Ask. Short answers only.

reply: what's on the clipboard? -> chat-ray-clip
reply: what's the counter doing? -> chat-ray-counter
reply: why the hoodie? -> chat-ray-hoodie
reply: never mind -> chat-ray-menu

node chat-ray-clip
kind: reply
pose: point

    A checklist.

    One: no hype. Two: no scare. Three: say what the sources say. Four: lunch.

    Four gets skipped. I'm working on it.

reply: lunch matters -> chat-ray-clip-lunch
reply: that's a good list -> chat-ray-talk

node chat-ray-clip-lunch
kind: reply
pose: proud

    Noted. Item four moves up to item two.

    Don't tell anyone.

react: haha -> chat-ray-talk
react: like -> chat-ray-talk

node chat-ray-counter
kind: reply
pose: think

    Hand-held. Goes everywhere I go.

    It reads something wherever I take it. Kitchen. Roof. Parking lot. That's normal. Background. Lesson four.

reply: so it's never zero? -> chat-ray-counter-zero
reply: ok -> chat-ray-talk

node chat-ray-counter-zero
kind: reply
pose: explain

    A working detector picks up a little almost anywhere. Background radiation is always there.

    Check the lesson if you want the full version.

reply: got it -> chat-ray-talk
reply: back to the list -> chat-ray-menu

node chat-ray-hoodie
kind: reply
pose: greet

    Purple. Warm. Pockets.

    The clipboard doesn't fit in the pocket. I've tried. We don't discuss it.

sticker: nerd -> chat-ray-talk
sticker: star -> chat-ray-talk

node chat-ray-bye
kind: sign_off
pose: proud

    Noted. Go.

    Come back with a question. Short answer guaranteed.
